WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
Some important ins and outs in the 2024

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.902
presidential campaign,

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.304
namely, New Hampshire Republican Governor

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.106
Chris Sununu says he's staying out.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.573
But former

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.107
Vice President

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.441
Mike Pence is officially getting

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.709
in, filing paperwork

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.410
with the Federal Election

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.412
Commission ahead of a formal announcement

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.347
at Wednesday's CNN town hall.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.181
Also expected

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.149
to declare this week, former

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:16.583
New Jersey

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.550
Governor Chris Christie

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.752
and South Carolina Senator Tim

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.453
Scott himself a Republican hopeful.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.688
He made headlines

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.622
for a contentious moment

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.823
today on The View.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:24.524
You're some of it,

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.458
which comes several weeks

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.993
after co-host Joy Behar,

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.594
Sunny Hostin,

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.262
Whoopi Goldberg made comments suggesting

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.096
that Scott

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.064
does not understand

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.099
or acknowledge systemic racism.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.234
Senator Scott also got booed

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.702
when talking about candidate

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:39.172
Ron DeSantis and his battle with Disney

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.774
One of the reasons why I'm on the show

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:41.741
is because of the comments

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.475
that were made, frankly,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.044
on this show, that the only way

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:44.711
for a young

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.645
African-American kid

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.347
to be successful in this country

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.382
is to be the exception. And not the rule.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.550
That is a dangerous,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.718
offensive,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:52.819
disgusting message

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.421
to send to our young people today,

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.457
that the only way to succeed is by being

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.159
the exception.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.427
I think Disney and Ron

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.529
have been in a combat zone

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.297
for a number of months over

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.466
what I thought was the right issue

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.468
as it relates to our young kids.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.102
And what they're

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.170
being indoctrinated with.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.805
I thought he started off on the

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.007
on the right foot on that issue. It is

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.576
no, no, no, no.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.078
Not Hey, I'm sorry, sir.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.279
Do not boo.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.481
This is the view we accept.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.450
We don't have to believe everything

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:23.917
people say,

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.952
but you cannot boo people here. Please.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.587
You cannot do it.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.922
Busy day in the presidential race.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:29.522
Joining us, CNN

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.323
political commentator

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:31.491
South Carolinian Bakari

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.826
Sellers, also Mark McKinnon.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.127
He's a columnist for The Daily Beast

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.995
and served as a campaign media adviser

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.164
to former President George W Bush.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.132
Because you're a little bit

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.868
of Senator Scott's perspective there.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:42.802
What do you make of it?

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:42.902
Well,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.037
I think it was actually

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.238
a good political strategy

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:45.672
to kind of go

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.340
into the belly of the beast.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.909
I think that Senator Scott uses

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.377
and I love Senator Scott.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.446
We're friends I would like to believe.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.314
I served with him

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.448
for four years in the South

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.549
Carolina legislative body.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.452
And as I like to say, I

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.753
would give Senator Scott a kidney.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.055
I just would never vote for him.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.157
But I think today is was a good day.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.593
To show you how nimble he is.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.094
I think he has a hard time

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.796
because he has an amazing story.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.663
He believes his story

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.731
to be the story of America.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.398
However,

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.234
he himself acknowledges that he is here

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.869
because he's a miracle.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:16.636
That in itself

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.371
means that there is some basic tenets

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.973
of systemic racism in the country.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.241
He refuses to acknowledge it.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:21.841
And I think that.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.909
Is that a political thing,

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.044
do you think, or is it an actual belief?

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:27.547
Oh, that's a good question, Anderson.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.149
I think it's a combination of both.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.551
I think for him, it may be a belief.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.552
I think for Nikki

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.487
Haley is probably more of a calculation,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.689
regardless of whatever

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.191
the foundation for that belief is.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.659
I think that is dangerous.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.593
I think when you acknowledge

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.461
yourself to be

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.263
I am here because I am an exception

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:43.696
I am here

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.932
because I am a miracle in this country,

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.301
than that in and of itself means that

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:49.802
there are some issues

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.470
that hold other people

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.971
who look like you back.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:52.338
Mark,

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.973
what is the lane

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.574
for Tim

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.376
Scott or Nikki Haley to become president?

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.377
Is it to try to stay

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.411
in the good graces of Trump

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.413
as long as possible for his base

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.281
while getting established?

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.249
Republican, Republicans and independents

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.886
Well, I think the lane is a lane

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.887
where you

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.422
you appeal to Republicans

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.492
who want a normal Republican Party.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:12.992
Again,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.594
and want to put Trump

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.662
in the rearview mirror.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.597
Now, I think, first of all, Nikki

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.965
Haley is a very deft

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.867
campaigner, did a great job on your town

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.702
hall, showed her experience

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.938
showed her unflappable ability

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:25.705
and to just show

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.507
she's kind of a normal Republican.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.008
A little bit of a throwback now.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.310
You know, is that going to appeal

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.744
to Trump base voters?

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.446
Probably not.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.081
But but there's room for others

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:35.682
in this race.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.617
And Tim Scott, by the way,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.119
as he has a lot of potential appeal

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:40.887
for Iowa

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.422
and Iowa, as we know,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.791
can completely shake up this race.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.358
And, you know,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.492
what people should be focusing on

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.860
is not the national polls,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.495
but what's happening in Iowa.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.232
And Tim Scott's got a very sunny Reagan

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.766
George Bush, compassionate,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.069
conservative, optimistic kind of message.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.538
And by the way, the thing I like about

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.139
that is an interesting debate

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:00.673
on the issue

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.442
that Bakari was talking about,

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.077
that we'll talk about

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.612
during this election.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.479
But what I like that

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:09.482
he's doing is that contrary to the Santas

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:09.983
and Trump,

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.484
who want to

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:12.752
claim that they are victims

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.319
and their voters

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.388
are victims of everything,

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.023
Tim Scott saying, I'm not a victim

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:17.890
and I like that.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.626
And I think a lot of Americans like that.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.394
They like that kind of Reagan

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.129
I know

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.998
you can be anything in this country now.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.266
Again, that's a debate we can have

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.934
and whether or not is fair to everybody.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.335
But it's a good message

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.771
and it appeals to all time to staff

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.872
and Republicans

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.274
and people in Ireland like me.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.375
Is that enough? I don't know.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.242
But it could be enough

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.577
to break through in Iowa.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.444
And once that happens,

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.579
that gets reshuffled.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:39.879
Yeah.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:40.380
I mean, Booker,

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.681
with the exception of Governor Sanders,

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:44.183
the former president, has been

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.352
relatively hands off

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.688
and even complimentary with Tim Scott.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:51.090
Nikki Haley, a clearly

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.558
he sees it as a benefit

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:52.925
to him

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:53.693
to have as many people

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.594
as possible in this race.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.228
Well, the problem

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.629
that most Americans don't realize

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.964
or most Republicans don't realize,

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.332
it's a structural problem

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.700
within the Republican Party.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.601
Is they didn't go back

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.669
and change the structure

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.903
of their primaries.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:04.570
So basically,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.039
when somebody wins the primary,

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:06.706
even if they win it

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.841
with 25 or 30% of the vote,

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.811
they they get all of those delegates to

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.780
to be the next nominee for president.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.081
So the more people who are in the race,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.949
the more benefits Donald Trump.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:17.383
I would

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.451
I would also say that

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.053
there is no benefit to Donald Trump.

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.788
For going after somebody

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.356
is, as Mark said,

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.290
with the disposition

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:24.691
of somebody

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.491
like Tim Scott,

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.926
people like Tim Scott,

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.695
he's genuinely likable.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.228
You feel like

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.030
although you may disagree with him,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:31.631
he's in it

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.932
because he believes in

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:33.900
what Abraham Lincoln called

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.768
the better angels of our nature.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.837
It's very difficult to go after him now.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:38.171
I think

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:38.838
when he has people

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.339
come in the race

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.673
like Mike Pence, who I believe

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.941
is getting in the race soon,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.476
or somebody like Chris Christie,

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.510
he won't have a choice

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:44.944
because they're going

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.379
to be throwing punches at him.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.715
I also David Axelrod said it last night

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:49.482
and I agree with him,

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.084
I don't think that Donald Trump's

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.151
going to engage much.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.720
I don't think he's going to debate much.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.921
I think it would be silly for him

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.923
to because he's just that far ahead.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.558
And if Donald Trump wins,

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.726
I would love to hear what Mark says.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.861
But if Donald Trump wins Iowa,

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.262
the rest of this is academic.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:06.032
I mean, he will be the nominee.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:08.568
Marc, do you think it makes any sense for

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:09.669
Trump to debate

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.372
or to engage?

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.040
Well, listen, I

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.241
think it makes sense for him to debate

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:15.842
because he

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.977
he dominates every debate that he's in

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.712
and just crushes everybody.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.315
I mean, we saw that in 2016.

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.816
I don't think he needs to engage

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.151
with the other candidates.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.886
I mean, it only elevates them

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:27.887
when he does.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.122
But I think personally,

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.590
who had the right message today

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.225
and what he said,

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:32.492
I mean,

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:33.426
first of all,

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.427
he's going to have more impact

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:34.861
on this race

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:35.461
by getting out

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.829
and staying in New Hampshire

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.264
now is in play.

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:41.067
And like Iowa, you know,

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:44.237
this race can be completely rearranged.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:46.239
Just ask the guy who lost to John McCain

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.274
by 19 points after coming in there

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.976
in the first place with George W Bush

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:51.310
in South Carolina

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.746
turning around and like a 30 point

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.183
change over the course of 24 hours.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.384
So

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.052
but his point is the one that's right

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.155
which is the more people who the

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:03.423
the more it helps Trump.

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.491
And so people like Sununu are getting out

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.226
because the last thing that they want

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:10.363
is is Trump to emerge as the nominee.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.632
And clearly I mean

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:13.933
Chris Christie

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.601
is gearing up for confrontation

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.904
and based on his public comments,

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:20.773
DeSantis is increasingly getting into it.

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:23.509
Do you think it's necessary

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:25.077
do you think.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.480
Do you think that's wise so soon?

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.750
So I I'm not a conspiracy

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.684
theory theorist,

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.352
but I do have a conspiracy theory.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.987
I think that there were some donors

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:35.321
who, by the way,

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:36.022
every conspiracy

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:37.423
theorist says are seriously there.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:38.858
I'm glad I'm not the world is flat.

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:39.659
But no.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.227
So I think people got together

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:42.061
and said, look,

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:42.962
Chris Christie,

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:44.397
go out and do to Donald Trump

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.798
what you did to Marco Rubio.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:46.833
I mean, kamikaze

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:48.601
Christie is coming in with one mission.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:49.302
There's no

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:51.437
way in hell Chris Christie believes

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.272
he can be president of the United States.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.674
I just do not.

